      "text": "Singer Yo Yo Honey Singh on Thursday told the Delhi high court that he did not perform the controversial song “Volume 1” during a 2025 concert in Delhi, after the court ordered the track to be taken down from all platforms over its allegedly vulgar and misogynistic lyrics.\n\nHoney Singh’s counsel, Rajshekhar Rao, on Thursday informed the court that his client did not perform the track at a concert held in Delhi in March last year.\n\nThe controversial song was released by the singers in 2006-07 under their collaboration titled Mafia Mundeer.\n\nKnow more 🔗 https://www.hindustantimes.com/india-news/stigma-must-go-didn-t-sing-it-singer-honey-singh-tells-hc-on-volume-1-row-101778155337232.html",
